Q: Multiple input variables - can only get 1 variable to pass A: <p>the sp_executesql stored procedure only takes one parameter definition string. so define boht parameters in the one string and then pass their values. follow the sammple:</p>
<pre><code>DECLARE @strSQL NVARCHAR(MAX); 
SET @strSQL = N' SELECT * FROM HumanResources.Department WHERE Name = @Name1 UNION ALL SELECT * FROM HumanResources.Department WHERE Name = @Name2;';
EXEC sys.sp_executesql @strSQL, N'@Name1 NVARCHAR(50), @Name2 NVARCHAR(50)', @Name1 = N'Engineering', @Name2 = N'Tool Design';
</code></pre>
<p>the main and your issue is that this part : <code>N'@Name2 nvarchar(max)'</code></p>
<p>is being passed as a value and not as another parameter definition. all pararmeter definitions need to be inside the same stringe separated by commmas.</p>

Q: Root detection Implementation can be bypassed using Magisk hide : Android App vulnerability A: <p>You can use this piece of code to detect magisk hide, use it in combination with another root detection lib like root beer. Here we are just going through all of the apps installed and searching for magisk specific lib names such as &quot;libstub.so&quot;.</p>
<pre><code>private void searchForMagisk() {
    PackageManager pm = getPackageManager();
    @SuppressLint(&quot;QueryPermissionsNeeded&quot;) List&lt;PackageInfo&gt; installedPackages = pm.getInstalledPackages(0);

    for (int i = 0; i &lt; installedPackages.size(); i++) {
        PackageInfo info = installedPackages.get(i);
        ApplicationInfo appInfo = info.applicationInfo;

        String nativeLibraryDir = appInfo.nativeLibraryDir;
        String packageName = appInfo.packageName;

        Log.i(&quot;Magisk Detection&quot;, &quot;Checking App: &quot; + nativeLibraryDir);

        File f = new File(nativeLibraryDir + &quot;/libstub.so&quot;);
        if (f.exists()) {
            ShowMessageBox(&quot;Magisk Detection&quot;, &quot;Magisk was Detected!&quot;);
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: Keycloak SSO Session Idle always set to 30 minutes A: <p>I faced the same issue from Client Side. After Refreshing Tokens in Client Side I was able to solve the issue. I used the following code. This could help. Kindly check.</p>
<pre><code>keycloak.onTokenExpired = () =&gt; {
   console.log(&quot;&gt;&gt;&gt; Re-Authenticated&quot;);
   keycloak.updateToken(50);
};
</code></pre>
